# =============================================================================
# OS/7 - line endings
#
# OS/7 is a Linux. Every executable text file in this repo is read by a Linux:
# by `env` resolving a shebang, by live-build running config/hooks/*.chroot
# inside the chroot, by GNU make, by dotnet, by pwsh. A CR before the newline
# is not whitespace to any of them - it is part of the interpreter's name.
#
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its SYSTEM config
# (C:/Program Files/Git/etc/gitconfig). Nothing in this repo's history contains
# a CR byte; the damage is done on CHECKOUT, so it is invisible to `git status`
# and to every diff. The symptom is:
#
#     env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#     env: use -[v]S to pass options in shebang lines
#
# `eol=lf` here OVERRIDES core.autocrlf, so the repo defends itself on any
# clone rather than depending on how each machine's Git was installed.
# docs/BUILD-NOTES.md #70.
# =============================================================================

# Everything Git detects as text is LF in the working tree, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Recorded real output is EVIDENCE and must stay byte-exact. run-zfs.py capture
# writes these from a live ZFS; the serial-console harness speaks CR on purpose
# (BUILD-NOTES #16). Never let an end-of-line filter edit a measurement.
#
# The Directory line names the same kind of evidence: `ldapsearch -o
# ldif-wrap=no` output taken off a real domain controller, beside the JSON each
# one was transcribed into. Without it `* text=auto` above decides those files'
# line endings on the first checkout that ever sees them, and a filter that has
# already run cannot be un-run from a .gitattributes.
powershell/Zfs/tests/fixtures/**        -text
powershell/Directory/tests/fixtures/**  -text
docs/SESSION-*.md                       -text

# Binaries, should any land here. `text=auto` guesses; these do not need to be
# guessed at. Fonts and images are built into the ISO byte-for-byte.
*.psf   binary
*.psfu  binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.deb   binary
*.png   binary
*.gz    binary
*.xz    binary
*.img   binary
*.iso   binary
